      "attack": "Probe the in-flight gauge for leaks on abnormal exit",
      "method": "Examine S6 AC2 ('when processing finishes, whether it succeeds or fails'). Ask what happens when processing throws, is cancelled, or times out.",
      "result": "Weakened. The AC never requires the decrement to run in a finally path, so an exception or cancellation can leave the gauge permanently elevated and trigger false in-flight alerts."
    },
    {
      "attack": "Check whether the disabled-path criteria are observable",
      "method": "Examine S2 AC2: 'no /metrics route exists and the request is not handled by a metrics handler'. Try to write a test from it.",
      "result": "Weakened. 'Not handled by a metrics handler' has no observable expected result. It should specify the status code (e.g. 404) and that the route is absent from the registered routes."
    },
    {
      "attack": "Check that the enabled path wires the real recorder",
      "method": "Look for an AC proving that with metrics.enabled=true the JobConsumer receives the real MetricsRecorder rather than the no-op. S2 AC3 covers only the disabled case.",
      "result": "Gap. The default configuration, which is the one that ships, has no AC confirming that S4-S6 record anything at all."
    },
    {
      "attack": "Check whether the alerting criteria are testable",
      "method": "Examine S8: the thresholds are 'configured' but no value, source, or lane label scheme is given. Evaluate S8 AC2 ('no alert fires') as a test.",
      "result": "Weakened. AC2 passes trivially when nothing is wired. AC1 cannot be run without a defined threshold."
    },
    {
      "attack": "Check the exposure risk of serving /metrics on the shared HTTP port",
      "method": "Look for any AC covering who can reach /metrics, binding, or authentication. The endpoint shares the port with /health and the service's other routes.",
      "result": "Gap. Nothing addresses whether metrics are exposed beyond the scraper network. Internal job and lane detail may leak."
    },
    {
      "attack": "Check the 'same simpleclient the sibling services use' claim",
      "method": "Look for evidence in the breakdown or triage that Apollo and Hermes use the same library and version, beyond the body's assertion.",
      "result": "Unverified. The breakdown restates the body's claim without confirming it, so the library choice and version compatibility are assumed."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "finding": "E3 (S7, S8) contradicts the triage correction and is out of scope for HP-12.",
      "evidence": "Triage: domains [backend]; rationale says 'the scrape side is not in scope here'. Breakdown: S7 and S8 have domains [infra] and describe dashboards and alerting."
    },
    {
      "finding": "E3 adds work the work item body never requested.",
      "evidence": "Body asks for: GET /metrics, metrics.enabled toggle, JVM metrics, and worker metrics via MetricsRecorder. It does not mention dashboards or alerting rules."
    },
    {
      "finding": "E1's title promises scrape-side work that the story set does not deliver.",
      "evidence": "E1 title: 'Operator can scrape Hephaestus's /metrics endpoint'. Its stories S1-S3 cover the endpoint and toggle only; Prometheus scrape configuration is not included, and the triage excludes it."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The histogram spec is missing the lane label and buckets that S7 depends on.",
      "evidence": "S5 specifies a processing-time histogram with no labels or buckets. S7 AC2 requires 'the histogram's quantiles are rendered per lane'."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The in-flight gauge has no guaranteed decrement on exceptional exit.",
      "evidence": "S6 AC2: 'when processing finishes, whether it succeeds or fails'. No AC covers exception, cancellation, or timeout paths."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The outcome label set is incomplete.",
      "evidence": "S4 AC1/AC2 define only outcome=success and outcome=failure. No other terminal outcome is specified."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The disabled-path AC has no observable expected result.",
      "evidence": "S2 AC2: 'the request is not handled by a metrics handler'. No status code or route-table assertion is given."
    },
    {
      "finding": "No AC verifies the enabled-path recorder wiring.",
      "evidence": "S2 AC3 covers only metrics.enabled=false ('a no-op MetricsRecorder is used'). Nothing asserts that the real recorder is injected by default."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The alert ACs are underspecified and S8 AC2 is trivially satisfiable.",
      "evidence": "S8: 'its configured threshold' with no value or source. AC2 'no alert fires' passes whenever no rule exists."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Exposure of /metrics on the shared HTTP port is not addressed.",
      "evidence": "S1 AC1 requires the route on 'the existing HTTP port' with no bind, network, or auth criteria."
    }
  ]
}
```

**Recommendation:** Keep E1 (S1-S3) and E2 (S4-S6) with the fixes above, but drop E3 or move it to a separate infra item, since the triage excludes it. Retitle E1 to cover the endpoint rather than scraping. Add lane and bucket definitions to S5, a finally-based decrement AC to S6, a full outcome set to S4, and a default-path wiring AC. The verdict is WEAKENED rather than REFUTED because the backend core survives the attacks; the failures are in scope, the infra stories, and several ACs that need tightening.

