      "evidence": "The body says 'when disabled there is no route and a no-op recorder'. S2 is the toggle story, but its two ACs test JVM metrics and text format, not the toggle. No AC asserts that /metrics is absent or that the recorder is a no-op when disabled."
    },
    {
      "finding": "S2 and S3 have duplicate acceptance criteria.",
      "evidence": "S2 AC1 ('the response includes base JVM metrics from the app CollectorRegistry') and S3 AC1 ('the response body includes base JVM metrics ... from the CollectorRegistry') assert the same thing under different stories."
    },
    {
      "finding": "The MetricsRecorder seam, its no-op implementation and its injection into JobConsumer have no owning story.",
      "evidence": "S4-S6 all depend on MetricsRecorder, but no story creates the interface, the no-op implementation or the wiring. The body says the seam is 'injected into the JobConsumer', which the breakdown does not cover."
